# Issue #933's guard, at the turtle: a newline between two complete commands still ends the first
# statement (`spec/grammar.md:34`), so this stays two instructions — one move, one turn — and never
# collapses into a single expression. `forward 100` then `right 90` is the shape every learner
# writes, so a fix that made expressions span newlines unconditionally would break it silently.
forward 100
right 90
